                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I recommend this game only to those who are really starved of first-person fantasy games.\n\nIt has some very good parts to it. It has good atmosphere. There is nice visual variety between levels. Some of the designs are quite creative.\n\nBut it is a slog of a game. The beginning is very difficult, but eventually you are given ranged weapons which makes the game trivial if you decide to use them. The tutorial really shows everything the game has to offer. Find keys, pull levers, get to a boss. Most of the bosses become common enemies you face shortly after, so none of them are memorable.\n\nMost of the game is linear, but then padded out with maze-like levels with very similar looking hallways. I don't know if the developer was trying to make the game seem longer than it is, but it made the experience worse, not better, and really hurt my lasting impression of the game. The linear levels play much better.\n\nI did finish the game, which is rare for me, so there is something here that's quite good. It took two lengthy sessions to complete. It has charm. I'm curious what the developers will make next.",
